  "covered_behaviors": [
    "Ten malformed event fixtures use top-level type values null, zero, false, an empty list and an empty object, each with a reasoning item and without an item. Every present nonstring type is rejected as invalid_event after canonical JSON validation.",
    "Four accepted controls retain prior behavior for item.started, an unknown provider.extension string, an empty type string and an absent type field.",
    "A valid agent response and valid usage follow each leading event. Malformed event rejection retains that later response and usage, persists a failed provider attempt and failed trial, and keeps monetary cost unknown.",
    "Raw event bytes and their SHA-256 commitments are retained exactly for both malformed fixtures and accepted controls.",
    "The broker makes one provider call despite a three-round limit. Malformed fixtures admit no usage charge or proposer actions and seal through harness abstention; accepted controls charge valid usage and submit and seal one proposal.",
    "The adjacent regression retains recognition of a started command_execution as an unapproved tool event, preserves a configuration warning as a diagnostic, and persists a failed attempt when mocked CLI discovery finds no provider executable."
  ],
